WEBVTT

00:00:17.890 --> 00:00:19.810
MOKICHI ROBINSON, FIGHTER OF SENTORY
(ELIMINATED)

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.650
KEIZABURO SAWADA
(ELIMINATED 1ST ROUND)

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:28.520
The crowd in the arena must be charged up.

00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:30.400
I can't contain my anger.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.150
YOSHIKO TOGAWA, PRESIDENT OF MURDER MUSIC

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:33.820
I'm sorry, Sawada.

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.160
This is all my fault
for not being cautious enough.

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:40.870
LIHITO OF SH FROZEN STORAGE

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.750
Lihito.

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:47.920
What? Did you come here to mock me
before your match tomorrow?

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:51.760
Sawada... who did this to you?

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:54.010
Oh, it was--

00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:55.970
Why do you ask?

00:00:56.340 --> 00:00:58.640
Are you going to avenge me or something?

00:00:59.050 --> 00:00:59.970
Sawada?

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.600
Don't underestimate me, prick.

00:01:03.770 --> 00:01:06.440
Your sympathy is no different
from an insult to me.

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.150
To us fighters,
results are all that matters.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.440
We don't need to cozy up to one another
like ordinary people!

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:18.450
Yoshiko, you shouldn't
feel responsible for me, either.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:21.580
I just fought of my own free will, okay?

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:22.910
Sawada...

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:24.040
Just wait and see.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.170
Once I've healed up,
I'm going to get my revenge on them.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.090
Sawada.

00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:33.340
I'm on it. Leave it to me.

00:01:33.630 --> 00:01:35.720
I promise I'll win this tournament.

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:39.220
I'll get your revenge on them.

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.510
<i>Oh, my goodness.</i>
<i>Did you even hear a word I just said?</i>

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:45.310
<i>I don't want you to fight for me.</i>

00:01:45.390 --> 00:01:48.440
<i>And besides, winning this tournament</i>
<i>has nothing to do with revenge.</i>

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:51.650
<i>I knew you were stupid,</i>
<i>but this is beyond my understanding!</i>

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:58.200
<i>But I guess, at least,</i>
<i>you're much better than the Toyo fellas.</i>

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:02.410
Hey, don't touch me! I'm injured.

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:04.160
Oh, sorry.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:06.790
They're such good friends, huh, Doctor?

00:02:06.870 --> 00:02:09.000
K. YOSHIZAWA & H. HANAFUSA, NURSE
& FIGHTER OF TEITO UNI

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.630
I'm glad that the medical office is
getting pretty noisy.

00:02:12.290 --> 00:02:16.550
I can't wait to have
another patient tomorrow.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:17.840
That's enough, Doctor.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:52.940
"MASTER AND PUPIL"

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:02.780
ADAM DUDLEY, REP. FIGHTER OF BOSS BURGER
(ELIMINATED IN THE FIRST ROUND)

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.700
Why the hell
do I have to eat with you guys?

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:10.700
There's something
I wanted to tell you in person.

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:12.460
COSMO IMAI, FIGHTER
NISHIHONJI SECURITY

00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:14.000
AKIRA NISHIHONJI
PRESIDENT

00:04:14.080 --> 00:04:15.420
You really are strong.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.170
I'm the winner this time, though.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.550
Are you picking a fight with me?

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:25.800
I admit, I was close to the edge
and I like your fighting style.

00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:27.930
I hope we get to fight again.

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:34.310
You don't need to tell me.
I'll beat you in a rematch soon.

00:04:34.690 --> 00:04:37.770
Don't lose to anybody
before I get to crush you!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.070
All right. Thank you.

00:04:44.070 --> 00:04:45.530
You're throwing me off.

00:04:45.950 --> 00:04:46.870
This is delicious.

00:04:46.990 --> 00:04:47.950
Yeah.

00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:51.080
We won't lack of anything
as long as we're on this island.

00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:54.080
Oceans of money are put
into this tournament.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.750
I guess preparing fancy meals
is nothing for them.

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:01.590
Well, I'll enjoy it for today.

00:05:02.010 --> 00:05:05.340
Cos, eat a lot and get ready
for the next match.

00:05:09.180 --> 00:05:11.770
He's a totally different person
from when he was fighting.

00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:15.770
Ow, it hurts...

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:17.060
What?

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:18.730
You're being too dramatic.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.230
It hurts where you hit me, Adam.

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:25.150
Are you okay, Cos?
Will you go to the doctor's office?

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:27.700
Yeah. I'll go get some painkillers.

00:05:28.570 --> 00:05:29.660
Seriously?

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.240
He got way too excited.

00:05:32.450 --> 00:05:35.660
It's not something the person
responsible for his injury should say.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.920
Yeah!

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:39.420
KAOLAN WONGSAWAT
FIGHTER

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:42.550
Hey, come on!

00:05:42.710 --> 00:05:44.460
What do you mean
my match is tomorrow, Kaolan?

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.680
SAW PAING YOROIZUKA
REP. FIGHTER OF VILLAGE OF DAWN

00:05:46.930 --> 00:05:48.840
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:05:49.010 --> 00:05:51.680
Not all the first-round matches
happen in one day.

00:05:51.890 --> 00:05:53.270
Is that so?

00:05:53.390 --> 00:05:56.430
Bummer! My body's already
completely warmed up.

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.730
Then stay warmed up.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.860
Your match is the first one tomorrow.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:03.400
All right! Yeah!

00:06:03.530 --> 00:06:06.900
Then, I'll eat a lot
and prepare for tomorrow!

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:10.070
<i>He's too enthusiastic as always.</i>

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:12.200
<i>But Saw Paing,</i>

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.700
<i>I'm going be the one</i>
<i>who wins this tournament.</i>

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:17.790
<i>No one can stop me from winning.</i>

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:29.010
My, this is such a lovely place.
I wonder if it's Mr. Katahara's taste.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.090
RINO KURAYOSHI
CHAIRWOMAN OF GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:35.600
REI MIKAZUCHI, REP. FIGHTER
OF GOLD PLEASURE GROUP

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:40.690
Oh, it seems like Rei's having fun.

00:06:41.650 --> 00:06:45.360
You're so relaxed
even before having your match, Rino.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:47.360
TOMARI TOHGO
PRESIDENT OF IWAMI HEAVY IND.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:50.070
Well, well. It's you, Ms. Tohgo.
Congratulations on your victory

00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:52.370
-in the first round.
-I take our victory for granted.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:55.870
The right to designate the chairman of
Kengan Association is going to be mine.

00:06:56.750 --> 00:06:59.250
And you're going to be
the chairman, right?

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.790
You're a hard worker, Tomari.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:08.880
I admit your fighter
is pretty high-level, too.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:11.930
<i>But our Muteba is a monster</i>
<i>who is even stronger than him.</i>

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.140
MUTEBA GIZENGA, REP. FIGHTER
OF IWAMI HEAVY INDUSTRIES

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:18.100
<i>I suppose today's match</i>
<i>taught you that very well.</i>

00:07:18.640 --> 00:07:20.890
Hey, Rino!

00:07:21.140 --> 00:07:24.020
Rei, I'll join you in a minute, okay?

00:07:25.150 --> 00:07:28.780
You'd better pray that your boyfriend
won't be killed in the next round.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:33.320
You seem really sure about your winning.
But no.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:37.540
I'm not going to let anyone destroy Rei.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:40.290
W-- What the hell
do you think you are doing?

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:43.290
Your skill should only
be used on guys.

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.710
Make eyes at men, not me.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:48.670
Oh. That's not true, actually.

00:07:49.130 --> 00:07:52.050
You know, I like women, too.

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.510
Ah, don't touch me!

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:58.260
Let's be friends, Tomari.

00:07:58.350 --> 00:08:00.350
Get off me.

00:08:00.430 --> 00:08:01.730
You're disgusting.

00:08:01.850 --> 00:08:03.690
Aw, that's boring.

00:08:07.860 --> 00:08:10.570
Mokichi is all healed up?
That's great news.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.320
ELENA ROBINSON
SISTER OF MOKICHI

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:13.700
KARURA KURE, KURE FAMILY

00:08:13.780 --> 00:08:16.530
Yeah. Thank you for worrying about him.

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.950
That was Raian's fault.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.460
He's the Kure Family's black sheep.

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:24.710
I'm sorry, Elena.

00:08:25.040 --> 00:08:28.500
Don't be. You don't need
to say sorry, Karura.

00:08:30.420 --> 00:08:35.180
Oh, yes! I'm glad Karura found someone
her age in this tournament.

00:08:35.470 --> 00:08:37.010
It seems they've hit it off already.

00:08:37.180 --> 00:08:38.930
REICHI KURE, KURE FAMILY
ERIO KURE, PATRIARCH

00:08:39.010 --> 00:08:41.180
That's the younger sister
of Mokichi Robinson.

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:45.230
She must be feeling bad
for what Raian did.

00:08:45.440 --> 00:08:47.860
What a sweetheart she is.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:51.320
Girls should hang out with girls.

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:57.240
I shall kill any shit-bag
that gets close to Karura.

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.580
Grandfather.

00:09:00.160 --> 00:09:01.830
Is the shit-bag you're talking about...

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:11.210
OHMA TOKITA, REPRESENTATIVE FIGHTER
OF YAMASHITA CORPORATION

00:09:28.350 --> 00:09:29.270
Hey.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:30.860
Done already?

00:09:31.110 --> 00:09:33.610
You can still keep going, can't you, pops?

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:38.410
<i>The Immeasurable, Gozo Murobuchi!</i>

00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:46.710
INDESTRUCTIBLE

00:09:50.290 --> 00:09:53.590
<i>He drops his guard for an instant</i>
<i>when he does a jumping knee kick.</i>

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.340
<i>Now.</i>

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.690
You're next, Yankee prick.

00:10:07.810 --> 00:10:11.150
<i>The Emperor, Adam Dudley!</i>

00:10:13.320 --> 00:10:14.860
<i>An out-of-body experience.</i>

00:10:15.650 --> 00:10:19.820
<i>It is image training</i>
<i>while one's physical body is put to sleep.</i>

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:22.660
<i>Ever since he learned it</i>
<i>from Niko Tokita 14 years ago,</i>

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:27.040
<i>Ohma has been using</i>
<i>this out-of-body training method.</i>

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:31.790
<i>He sets an environment</i>
<i>exactly like the real world,</i>

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:35.090
<i>makes copies of the fighters,</i>
<i>and spars with them.</i>

00:10:35.460 --> 00:10:39.840
<i>Repetitive learning during sleep</i>
<i>affects the brain.</i>

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:41.720
<i>It's been scientifically proven.</i>

00:10:43.810 --> 00:10:45.180
<i>Eight matches.</i>

00:10:45.930 --> 00:10:51.190
<i>That's the average number of</i>
<i>imaginary matches Ohma fights per rest.</i>

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:56.230
<i>Eight matches times 365 days,</i>
<i>times 14 years.</i>

00:10:56.690 --> 00:11:00.360
<i>Fighting over 40,000 imaginary matches</i>

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:05.580
<i>has enabled his brain</i>
<i>to act without thinking.</i>

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:10.000
REDIRECTION KATA: WEEPING WILLOW

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:12.670
<i>I can't completely throw the trunk</i>
<i>of his body off balance.</i>

00:11:13.000 --> 00:11:15.210
<i>In that case, I'll just reverse his power.</i>

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:21.220
<i>The Redirection Kata: Entanglement.</i>

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:22.550
<i>And then...</i>

00:11:24.350 --> 00:11:26.930
ADAMANTINE KATA: IRONBREAKER

00:11:32.020 --> 00:11:32.900
Good.

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:35.690
<i>Wow, look who's gotten stronger.</i>

00:11:35.770 --> 00:11:36.730
What?

00:11:40.070 --> 00:11:42.910
<i>It seems you've been keeping up</i>
<i>with your training.</i>

00:11:43.240 --> 00:11:44.870
<i>I'm impressed.</i>

00:11:45.120 --> 00:11:47.700
<i>But I can't give you full marks.</i>

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:51.710
<i>Your training means nothing</i>
<i>if you have them as your opponents.</i>

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:54.040
<i>What is he doing here?</i>

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:56.710
<i>Look how much you've grown, Ohma.</i>

00:11:57.380 --> 00:11:59.760
<i>I'm your next opponent.</i>

00:12:00.010 --> 00:12:02.720
What the hell are you doing here,

00:12:03.430 --> 00:12:04.340
Niko?

00:12:07.430 --> 00:12:08.310
Hey.

00:12:08.810 --> 00:12:11.680
It's been so long, hasn't it?

00:12:12.190 --> 00:12:13.980
NIKO TOKITA, OHMA'S MASTER OF NIKO STYLE

00:12:14.150 --> 00:12:18.650
<i>I thought I'd suppressed my consciousness</i>
<i>so that he wouldn't show up.</i>

00:12:18.860 --> 00:12:23.240
It seems you've gotten better at
the out-of-body experience I taught you.

00:12:23.450 --> 00:12:28.740
You've set the same levels of fatigue,
damage, and everything as in reality.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:32.910
However, this training is not
good enough for you.

00:12:33.620 --> 00:12:34.920
What do you mean?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.210
What do you think I mean?

00:12:41.130 --> 00:12:43.680
I'm talking about these two
you were playing with.

00:12:45.220 --> 00:12:47.800
Gozo Murobuchi and Adam Dudley.

00:12:48.220 --> 00:12:52.560
You only know
a small fraction of their strategies.

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:57.560
You have too little information
to draw out their true power.

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:00.190
Same for me.

00:13:00.360 --> 00:13:03.030
I'm not quite
the real Niko Tokita myself.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:08.450
I'm just a phantom of Niko Tokita
created by your memories.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:13.450
Simply put, I'm like your inner voice.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.040
That's why I don't use difficult words
like the real Niko would do.

00:13:18.630 --> 00:13:20.460
Because you're stupid.

00:13:25.260 --> 00:13:26.130
So?

00:13:28.640 --> 00:13:32.350
Did you come here just to tell me that?

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:35.730
Well, let's forget about the details.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.860
The man who knows you best
is right in front of you.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:47.110
What better opponent could you ask for?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.950
So, what are you going to do, runt?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.340
Fine by me.

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:07.090
You want to get your ass kicked
by your own Niko Style?

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.970
Get my ass kicked?

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:13.010
You shouldn't say out loud
something you can't do.

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:16.770
You'll see if I can or cannot.

00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.900
NIKO STYLE

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.310
ADAMANTINE &
FLAME KATAS

00:14:22.190 --> 00:14:23.820
FLASHING STEEL: BLAST

00:14:27.950 --> 00:14:30.070
Your Flame Kata is passable.

00:14:30.570 --> 00:14:35.200
But you're still as awful as ever
at the Adamantine Kata.

00:14:35.870 --> 00:14:38.370
Flashing Steel is
a combination of two techniques,

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:42.420
Raging Fire of the Flame Kata
and Indestructible of the Adamantine Kata.

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:44.300
Speaking of which,

00:14:44.960 --> 00:14:48.550
didn't you use Flashing Steel
against Jerry Tyson during the prelim?

00:14:49.680 --> 00:14:53.260
You were lucky.
Your opponent was weak.

00:14:58.180 --> 00:14:59.270
Good grief.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:01.850
ADAMANTINE & FLAME KATAS

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:05.360
FLASHING STEEL: SMASH

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:13.530
It's true that Flashing Steel is
the Niko Style's fastest offensive move.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:17.660
But its movement is very linear.

00:15:17.950 --> 00:15:18.870
Hence...

00:15:20.540 --> 00:15:22.330
that makes it predictable.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.090
The Adamantine Kata technique,
Iron Fingers.

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:28.630
It's originally for cutting
the opponent deep to the quick

00:15:28.760 --> 00:15:31.050
by hardening the finger joints
with your muscles.

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:35.760
But if you use it this way,
you can easily crush their bones.

00:15:36.470 --> 00:15:39.100
Remember what I told you
when you were a kid?

00:15:39.600 --> 00:15:42.020
The application makes the technique.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:45.900
You rely on big, flashy moves too much.

00:15:48.280 --> 00:15:50.780
REDIRECTION KATA: WEEPING WILLOW

00:15:52.280 --> 00:15:53.990
WATER KATA: BIND OF PISCES

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:54.990
Phew.

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.330
That was a close call.

00:15:57.830 --> 00:16:01.660
But Weeping Willow's just a move
to throw the opponent off balance.

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:03.370
Don't trust it too much.

00:16:03.790 --> 00:16:08.170
The Water Kata is another one
you were poor at, isn't it?

00:16:09.010 --> 00:16:11.170
How many times do I have to tell you?

00:16:11.840 --> 00:16:15.090
You know the true Niko Style
only if you've mastered all four katas.

00:16:15.220 --> 00:16:17.510
NIKO-STYLE DIAGRAM
FLAME - REDIRECTION - WATER - ADAMANTINE

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:20.310
You rely way too much on
Redirection and Flame Katas.

00:16:21.890 --> 00:16:24.310
You're talking nonsense.

00:16:26.730 --> 00:16:28.730
Oh. There we go.

00:16:29.280 --> 00:16:31.740
You always resort to that
whenever you're cornered.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:34.240
That's so dull, you know.

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:35.870
Well, all right.

00:16:36.120 --> 00:16:38.530
There are no limits in this world.

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:41.080
Take out the "Advance"
as much as you like.

00:16:41.250 --> 00:16:42.620
Fine.

00:16:42.870 --> 00:16:44.710
You're talking too much.

00:16:45.040 --> 00:16:47.500
It's time for you to go away.

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:54.010
Strange, isn't it?

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:58.510
You've sped up quite a bit,
but I countered you so easily.

00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.060
You trust the "Advance" way too much.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:08.560
It increases your physical abilities,
in exchange for your delicate motions.

00:17:09.070 --> 00:17:12.690
That makes you unable to use
some techniques of the Niko Style.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:15.700
<i>It's very effective against</i>
<i>fighters like Ryo Inaba,</i>

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:17.950
<i>who's physically weaker than you.</i>

00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:23.200
<i>But you're not meant to use it against</i>
<i>someone like Jun Sekibayashi,</i>

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.420
<i>who's physically stronger than you.</i>
<i>As a matter of fact,</i>

00:17:26.710 --> 00:17:30.040
<i>you suffered heavy damage</i>
<i>in the match against Sekibayashi.</i>

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:32.050
That's not all.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:36.430
It is certain that
the "Advance" will kill you eventually.

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:40.350
-Son of a bitch.
-Don't rely on the "Advance" too much.

00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:43.600
Trust in my Niko Style.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:45.230
Shut up!

00:17:45.980 --> 00:17:49.480
Then why did you lose?

00:17:50.230 --> 00:17:52.610
You got killed...

00:17:53.530 --> 00:17:57.910
because you were weak!

00:17:58.820 --> 00:17:59.990
KAEDE AKIYAMA
KAZUO YAMASHITA

00:18:00.070 --> 00:18:02.540
-Ohma?
-Kazuo Yamashita.

00:18:02.910 --> 00:18:04.200
Kaede Akiyama.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.790
Are you all right?

00:18:05.960 --> 00:18:07.790
Did you have a bad dream?

00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:10.750
What are you doing, Kazuo Yamashita?

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.210
Oh, nothing.

00:18:13.460 --> 00:18:16.840
Your sudden screaming just scared me.

00:18:16.970 --> 00:18:20.430
Are you feeling okay?
I can take you to the doctor's office.

00:18:20.600 --> 00:18:21.850
Don't bother.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.020
Ohma...

00:18:27.020 --> 00:18:28.140
You're bleeding!

00:18:28.730 --> 00:18:31.650
That's way too much for just a nosebleed.

00:18:31.730 --> 00:18:34.190
Your internal organs might be damaged.

00:18:34.440 --> 00:18:37.450
We really should go to
the doctor's office, Ohma.

00:18:40.950 --> 00:18:43.120
It's not that big of a deal, you guys.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.660
My wounds just opened a little.

00:18:45.750 --> 00:18:46.830
Ohma!

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:49.920
I'll go wash my face.
Don't wait for me.

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:51.830
Ohma.

00:19:23.620 --> 00:19:26.160
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:30.580
<i>Could this be caused by the "Advance"?</i>

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:35.500
<i>Tch. It doesn't matter.</i>

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:40.550
<i>I just need to last long enough</i>
<i>to kill that cocksucker...</i>

00:19:41.180 --> 00:19:43.640
Setsuna Kiryu.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:46.720
That's all that matters to me.

00:19:51.270 --> 00:19:53.690
<i>Ladies and gentlemen!</i>

00:19:53.770 --> 00:19:57.690
<i>Did too much excitement</i>
<i>keep you awake last night?</i>

00:19:57.820 --> 00:19:58.980
KENGAN LIFE-OR-DEATH

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:03.070
<i>Thank you for your patience.</i>

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.330
<i>Kengan matches.</i>

00:20:16.130 --> 00:20:19.340
<i>That is an alternative form of war</i>
<i>between companies.</i>

00:20:20.010 --> 00:20:22.930
<i>They train for this day.</i>

00:20:23.510 --> 00:20:27.600
<i>They live for this stage.</i>

00:20:28.100 --> 00:20:33.640
<i>They fight with their true power</i>
<i>and techniques.</i>

00:20:33.940 --> 00:20:36.940
<i>Is it genuine violence?</i>

00:20:37.270 --> 00:20:39.650
<i>Or is it a refined martial art?</i>

00:20:40.230 --> 00:20:43.780
<i>The chosen ones are here to fight.</i>

00:20:44.450 --> 00:20:47.620
<i>Surge your blood, break your body,</i>

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:51.120
<i>and go beyond human limit.</i>

00:20:51.660 --> 00:20:54.830
<i>Then you'll get the right</i>
<i>to create new history.</i>

00:20:55.290 --> 00:20:57.880
<i>Who is the strongest?</i>

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:04.590
<i>This is the second day</i>
<i>of Kengan Life-or-Death Tournament!</i>

00:21:04.840 --> 00:21:08.510
<i>The first round of block C</i>
<i>officially begins now.</i>

00:21:10.510 --> 00:21:13.180
Thanks for coming with me, Karura.

00:21:13.390 --> 00:21:15.270
Don't mention it, Elena.

00:21:15.600 --> 00:21:17.810
That's what friends do, you know?

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.980
I'm sorry to cause you so much trouble.

00:21:21.280 --> 00:21:23.320
I'll be fine on my own now.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.360
You can go watch the matches.

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:30.160
No, I'll stick with you.
Ohma's not fighting today.

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:32.160
Who is Ohma?

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:36.790
He's the first man I've had a crush on.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:38.670
Wow. That's amazing.

00:21:38.750 --> 00:21:39.880
How about this, Elena?

00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:42.510
Why don't we go see Ohma
after checking on Mokichi?

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.670
-Sure.
-Let's go.

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:48.800
Ohma is such an incredible man.

00:21:48.890 --> 00:21:50.720
Ah. I'm sorry.

00:21:52.310 --> 00:21:53.180
SETSUNA KIRYU

00:21:53.310 --> 00:21:54.230
Are you okay?

00:21:55.060 --> 00:21:55.940
Yes.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:57.690
Good. Be careful.

00:22:00.770 --> 00:22:04.280
I won't blame you
if you just see him as your secret idol.

00:22:05.360 --> 00:22:07.030
Hey, Karura.

00:22:07.200 --> 00:22:09.990
He's so handsome, isn't he?

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:15.450
<i>What kind of man is he?</i>

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:17.710
<i>I couldn't feel his presence.</i>

00:22:18.370 --> 00:22:20.040
<i>I've never seen anyone like that.</i>

00:22:21.040 --> 00:22:24.590
<i>Is he even alive?</i>

00:22:25.510 --> 00:22:28.380
<i>I won't let anyone else have him.</i>

00:22:30.680 --> 00:22:33.680
<i>Ohma Tokita is mine.</i>

00:24:05.940 --> 00:24:06.820
PREVIEW

00:24:06.940 --> 00:24:08.690
<i>Yelling, howling, yelling, howling.</i>

00:24:09.030 --> 00:24:12.070
<i>Howling Fighting Spirit versus</i>
<i>the Giant of the Sea of Japan.</i>

00:24:12.530 --> 00:24:15.910
<i>Two men's pride crash on the shoreline.</i>

00:24:16.200 --> 00:24:17.790
<i>This match is not a frame-up!</i>

00:24:18.620 --> 00:24:20.160
<i>Next episode: "Fisherman."</i>

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:21.660
Subtitle translation by Miki Miyaji
